00:06:03.515 --> 00:06:05.930
- Tommy, thanks for the great question.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:09.436
Obviously, being one of the
great managers of all time

00:06:09.436 --> 00:06:11.746
this answer's gonna come
very easy to you and

00:06:11.746 --> 00:06:13.696
very natural, I think you'll get it.

00:06:13.696 --> 00:06:16.645
I spend a lot of time
thinking about motivation

00:06:16.645 --> 00:06:19.246
and I think the key for me is I try

00:06:19.246 --> 00:06:21.033
to motivate in a couple of ways.

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:23.390
Number one by example,
I think my actions will

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:25.410
always speak louder than my words so how I

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.732
carry myself, how I interact
with everybody, how I

00:06:27.732 --> 00:06:31.528
live my life as a man I
think really matters as an

00:06:31.528 --> 00:06:36.207
executive, as a person, I think
everyone's always watching.

00:06:36.207 --> 00:06:39.712
But I also think I equally
try to reverse engineer every

00:06:39.712 --> 00:06:42.108
single individual person, right.

00:06:42.108 --> 00:06:44.704
They're just all different,
they all have different KPIs,

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:46.504
different objectives,
they're in different parts of

00:06:46.504 --> 00:06:49.290
their lives, some are married
some just had kids, some are

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:51.553
trying to make more
money, some don't want to

00:06:51.553 --> 00:06:54.095
have four roommates in
Brooklyn, so they're grinding.

00:06:54.095 --> 00:06:56.555
So everybody's got a
different thing and I think

00:06:56.555 --> 00:06:59.425
what's important for me to
motivate is to do a great

00:06:59.425 --> 00:07:02.164
job listening to what makes
them tick, both when I

00:07:02.164 --> 00:07:04.463
have the few moments with them in person.

00:07:04.463 --> 00:07:07.117
Alex, get over here for a second.

00:07:07.117 --> 00:07:10.627
Let's do a real life example
on the #AskGaryVee Show.

00:07:10.627 --> 00:07:14.725
Alex, what motivates you,
what are you excited about?

00:07:14.725 --> 00:07:16.699
- What am I excited about? In life?

00:07:16.699 --> 00:07:18.347
- Yeah, what motivates you in life?

00:07:18.347 --> 00:07:22.312
- I just like doing cool
(beep), that's it pretty much.

00:07:23.164 --> 00:07:25.916
I want to be successful
and just do cool (beep),

00:07:25.916 --> 00:07:27.798
that's basically why I'm here so you know.

00:07:27.798 --> 00:07:28.981
- Cool man, alright, get out of here.

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:31.698
So, Alex is easy, he just
wants to do cool (beep).

00:07:31.698 --> 00:07:33.776
So that's easy, we do tons of cool (beep).

00:07:33.776 --> 00:07:35.680
He's check, he's good, he's motivated.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.165
And you go on and on and on and you

00:07:37.165 --> 00:07:39.882
try to figure out, was he
scared that he was on camera

00:07:39.882 --> 00:07:41.856
and is that the real
answer, like are they really

00:07:41.856 --> 00:07:44.642
gonna tell me the truth,
they never tell me the truth

00:07:44.642 --> 00:07:46.662
usually upfront, few and
far between and so it's

00:07:46.662 --> 00:07:50.562
a constant behavioral HR driven reverse

00:07:50.562 --> 00:07:52.501
engineering what they care about.

00:07:52.501 --> 00:07:55.159
India and I had a pretty
intense conversation

00:07:55.159 --> 00:07:58.700
about her future ambitions,
remember you wanted

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.337
to be the head of social
media for museums.

00:08:00.337 --> 00:08:03.019
I take that very seriously,
like I know these things

00:08:03.019 --> 00:08:05.061
about my peeps, this is
even before India was on

00:08:05.061 --> 00:08:07.282
the inner circle of this team, like I

00:08:07.842 --> 00:08:10.067
I remembered it 
better than you did.

00:08:10.067 --> 00:08:12.642
- Yeah, that's true, you did it's true.

00:08:12.642 --> 00:08:16.392
- So I take enormous,

00:08:16.392 --> 00:08:18.482
you don't get to be a great

00:08:18.482 --> 00:08:21.662
all time leader without being
a great all time leader.

00:08:21.662 --> 00:08:23.601
There's a lot of work that
gets put into being good

00:08:23.601 --> 00:08:27.757
at what I do and I'm very,
very up to the challenge

00:08:27.757 --> 00:08:30.404
and so it's predicated on an
enormous amount of listening

00:08:30.404 --> 00:08:33.664
which is why I'm such a
paradox because boy do I (beep)

00:08:33.664 --> 00:08:35.837
