of listening that I'm actually

00:08:35.837 --> 00:08:39.274
doing always surprises
people when they start going

00:08:39.274 --> 00:08:41.456
a couple of layers deeper so
the answer to your question

00:08:41.456 --> 00:08:44.776
is I motivate, Tommy, by
figuring out what every

00:08:44.776 --> 00:08:48.700
single person is ticked and wired like and

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:51.114
what makes them roll and I also recognize

00:08:51.114 --> 00:08:54.539
that that changes every
single day and they

00:08:54.539 --> 00:08:57.302
have four to seven, twelve
milestone things that

00:08:57.302 --> 00:08:59.380
happen in their lives,
which will change the

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:01.597
trajectory of their
ambitions, wants, hopes,

00:09:01.597 --> 00:09:03.676
and dreams and I need to be prepared for

00:09:03.676 --> 00:09:07.745
every single one of those
for all of them forever.

00:09:09.201 --> 00:09:11.467
- [Voiceover] Dylan asks "Do you
still believe that there's

00:09:11.467 --> 00:09:13.979
"integrity in the 
communications industry?"

00:09:14.739 --> 00:09:16.736
- Dylan I want to too
and I think the answer is

00:09:16.736 --> 00:09:19.394
there absolutely is but I
think that there's integrity,

00:09:19.394 --> 00:09:23.121
there's very little integrity
in every single market,

00:09:23.121 --> 00:09:26.882
advertising, politics, sports, music.

00:09:27.482 --> 00:09:30.933
The reason integrity is so
attractive is it's so hard.

00:09:30.933 --> 00:09:33.882
It's far and few between and
integrity's defined differently

00:09:33.882 --> 00:09:35.786
by everybody and I think
it's interesting to watch.

00:09:35.786 --> 00:09:37.887
I actually think society
is giving people more

00:09:37.887 --> 00:09:40.825
room to be flawed, which is intriguing.

00:09:40.825 --> 00:09:44.365
I think the level of
integrity, the way integrity is

00:09:44.365 --> 00:09:46.930
viewed upon today I
think is in a much better

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:49.427
place than it was by society
let's say 50 years ago

00:09:49.427 --> 00:09:51.469
because I think we're
now factoring in that

00:09:51.469 --> 00:09:53.327
nobody's perfect and we're making mistakes

00:09:53.327 --> 00:09:56.822
even by standards like
drugs and relationships

00:09:56.822 --> 00:09:59.271
and cheating, like intense
stuff, I think there's

00:09:59.271 --> 00:10:01.349
an interesting evolution and I think that

00:10:01.349 --> 00:10:03.961
that's allowed for a
little bit more gray and

00:10:03.961 --> 00:10:05.865
a little bit more if you're
really on your high horse

00:10:05.865 --> 00:10:08.547
creating a scenario where
you judge integrity.

00:10:08.547 --> 00:10:12.064
But I think in a lot of ways
there's plenty of integrity.

00:10:12.064 --> 00:10:14.467
I think there's a ton of
integrity out there still.

00:10:14.467 --> 00:10:16.859
